y+2=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "b42bfa467b538d9b8d7291413bd6a0bb059e06cb6a67a46b3c779b921a2e4ee1" "basis" 1163 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-77771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the line $y=-2x+3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063187/state.json" "file_sha256" "dc4e09064bdf4a84edd50fdaffb6950ec2445966b1b1ee62fee7f17be5c57f27"} {"question" "q-77771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the line $y=-2x+3$ passes through the points $U(0,3)$ and $V(1,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $U$ and $V$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${U}^{′}(-6,-3)$ and ${V}^{′}(-2,2).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${U}^{′}$ and ${V}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-3) & =\\frac{2-(-3)}{-2-(-6)}(x-(-6)) \\\\ y+3 & =\\frac{5}{4}(x+6) \\\\ 4y+12 & =5x+30 \\\\ 5x-4y+18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063187/state.json" "file_sha256" "dc4e09064bdf4a84edd50fdaffb6950ec2445966b1b1ee62fee7f17be5c57f27"} {"question" "q-77771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4d0c4894a8ccfc9acf716ef6bded90091d0da814b713a2069af3403fe6946ac1"} {"question" "q-77771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063187/state.json" "file_sha256" "dc4e09064bdf4a84edd50fdaffb6950ec2445966b1b1ee62fee7f17be5c57f27"} {"question" "q-77771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4x+5y+18=0"] ["math" "4x-5y+18=0"] ["math" "5x+2y+18=0"] ["math" "5x-2y+8=0"] ["math" "5x-4y+18=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063187/state.json" "file_sha256" "dc4e09064bdf4a84edd50fdaffb6950ec2445966b1b1ee62fee7f17be5c57f27"} {"question" "q-77771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x-4y+18=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063187/state.json" "file_sha256" "dc4e09064bdf4a84edd50fdaffb6950ec2445966b1b1ee62fee7f17be5c57f27"} {"question" "q-77776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the line $y=4x-1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation 